        {
          "topic": "Scope",
          "instructions": "A fictional comparison for an eight-year-old with professionally identified word-reading and classroom-participation needs. Every response range is an authored assumption, not a validated prediction or a confidence interval. Separate progress measures inform reconsideration; before-and-after change alone does not establish a causal effect."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Starting values",
          "instructions": "Prefilled values are fictional examples. Changing part of the workbook can leave example inputs in the case."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Editing",
          "instructions": "Edit the named input sheets. Keep worksheet names, column headers and record identifiers. Do not add formulas. Other case inputs remain unchanged."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Units and time",
          "instructions": "All response assumptions refer to the fictional six-week support horizon. Reading uses additional correct items on a declared 20-item probe; participation uses percentage-point change under a declared observation protocol; additional burden is minutes per week. No monetary conversion or probability is inferred. Null response bounds remain unknown. Sources, applicability, goals and priorities require qualified human judgment."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Import",
          "instructions": "Upload this workbook, inspect the changes and diagnostics, then apply. Importing does not calculate results or establish operating permission."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Sources and applicability",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Supply the declared case inputs. Published rules and other case context are retained."
        },
        {
          "topic": "Priorities",
          "instructions": "Editable inputs. Supply the declared case inputs. Published rules and other case context are retained."
